{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1135581-obligatory-supplements","id":1135581,"title":"Obligatory Supplements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-30T13:46:43-07:00","id":1135581,"title":"Obligatory Supplements","content":"It appears that Onyx Path is slowly but surely building up a set of \u201cstaple supplements\u201d for each gameline: books that the fans expect to be there, and sooner rather than later. As I see it, they are:<br /> <br /> \u00b7 a Player's Guide of some sort, dedicated to presenting a wider range of options for player characters.<br /> \u00b7 a Storyteller's Guide, dedicated to presenting the Storyteller with more options.<br /> \u00b7 a Night Horrors book, expanding the list of antagonists for the gameline.<br /> \u00b7 a Dark Era.<br /> \u00b7 an expansion to Mortal Remains, recasting the gameline through the eyes of Hunter: the Vigil.<br /> \u00b7 coming soon: a Contagion Chronicles expansion, addressing crossover issues with the other gamelines. <br /> <br /> Am I imagining things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:48:59-07:00","id":1135582,"title":"","content":"This cycle started in 1e, with the Big Three all getting their Chronicler's Guides and those three plus Changeling also got Night Horrors.<br /> <br /> Honestly? All I want is for the Storyteller's Guides to have Shards in the back like the phenomenal Demon one did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T17:32:10-07:00","id":1135639,"title":"","content":"Yea, that pretty much seems to be a thing. I just wish it'd been a little more streamlined in the production phase. Like you get it in a specific order: Core Book, Ready Made Characters, Storyteller's Guide, Player's Guide, Night Horrors, Mortal Remains, Dark Eras. But that's mostly because I'm really big on having a very tight order to things, and right now it feels like chaos with &quot;wait, what came out? and what is in that book?&quot; A separate Shards book would be nice too. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T22:29:18-07:00","id":1135678,"title":"","content":"...I know it's not strictly &quot;obligatory,&quot; but I really feel my completionist bug spasming when I see a line that doesn't get a conversion guide between it and its closest OWoD equivalent. I'm still hopeful that there will be a Geist/Wraith/Orpheus conversion guide, and a Changeling one (and maybe they could roll some Beast stuff into the Changeling one, seeing as it's so deeply entwined with human dreams and myths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T23:40:36-07:00","id":1135686,"title":"","content":"I see this pattern in now going gamelines - but I'm worried with it. For example, with announced for <b>Werewolf</b> 2E books <b>Tribes of Moon</b> ( asuming it's also book about Sacred Hunts and Tribes-Prey relation ) and <b>Night Horrors: Shuanted by Moon</b> - we get <i>almost</i> everything that is needed to run this game. 'Almost' is key word here. From 2E corebook we do not have rules for creating or running Hosts - that are 1/5 ( or 1/7 ) of Preys needed. Maybe they can be put in Storytellers book, but seems a bit ill-fit there.<br /> <br /> And we have also Mage 2E that seems to work on diffrent suppelmensts paradigm - with <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> and <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T02:20:14-07:00","id":1135701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1135581-obligatory-supplements?p=1135686#post1135686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see this pattern in now going gamelines - but I'm worried with it. For example, with announced for <b>Werewolf</b> 2E books <b>Tribes of Moon</b> ( asuming it's also book about Sacred Hunts and Tribes-Prey relation ) and <b>Night Horrors: Shuanted by Moon</b> - we get <i>almost</i> everything that is needed to run this game. 'Almost' is key word here. From 2E corebook we do not have rules for creating or running Hosts - that are 1/5 ( or 1/7 ) of Preys needed. Maybe they can be put in Storytellers book, but seems a bit ill-fit there.<br /> <br /> And we have also Mage 2E that seems to work on diffrent suppelmensts paradigm - with <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> and <b>Signs of Sorcery</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see them doing a third Werewolf Night Horrors book covering spirits and Hosts. Barring that, a Werewolf book focusing on the Shadow and its denizens could fulfill the same purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}